# Build context for docker/Dockerfile. The context is the REPO ROOT -- every
# service in docker-compose.yml declares `context: ..` from docker/ -- so this
# file lives here rather than in docker/, and one copy governs all three images.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS: without it the context was ~400 MB and Docker read all of it on
# every build. Five `execute` targets in the Makefile pass --build (it is not
# optional there -- the execute service does not mount src/, so a stale image
# would run yesterday's order logic against today's proposal), so this cost was
# paid several times per trading session.
#
# The Dockerfile COPYs exactly seven paths:
#     pyproject.toml uv.lock README.md LICENSE
#     src/ config/ prompts/ scripts/ tests/
# Anything not under those is dead weight in the context. Anything that IS
# cannot be excluded -- see the three warnings at the bottom.

# --- the big ones ---------------------------------------------------------- #
# Runtime state, mounted at ../data:/app/data. Never copied. The bars and GDELT
# caches live here and are the bulk of it.
data/
# The host virtualenv. The image builds its own at /opt/venv.
.venv/
# Agent session state -- and it contains a COMPLETE SECOND COPY of the repo
# under worktrees/, including its own src/research_desk. Nothing copies it and
# a stale duplicate tree has no business in a build layer.
.claude/
.git/
.gitignore
# Mounted at ../logs:/app/logs.
logs/

# --- caches and editor droppings ------------------------------------------- #
# NOTE THE `**/`. Docker matches these patterns against the ENTIRE relative
# path, unlike .gitignore which matches a bare name at any depth. A plain
# `__pycache__/` here would exclude only the one at the repo root and ship
# src/research_desk/__pycache__, tests/__pycache__ and scripts/__pycache__ --
# all three of which exist and all three of which land inside a COPY.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store
**/.ipynb_checkpoints
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.idea
.vscode

# --- secrets --------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Not copied, but a file of live credentials has no reason to be readable by a
# build at all. example.env is the committed template and stays.
.env
.env.*
!example.env

# --- documentation --------------------------------------------------------- #
# EXCLUDED BY NAME, NEVER BY *.md GLOB. See the README warning below.
tradingagents-architecture.md
tradingagents-migration-plan.md
FOLLOWUPS.md
CLAUDE.md
docs/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# DO NOT ADD THESE. Each one breaks the build, and two of the three fail with
# an error that does not name the cause.
#
#   tests/        -- `COPY tests/ ./tests/` is explicit. Excluding it fails the
#                    build outright. It is also load-bearing: the `dev` image
#                    runs the suite in-container, and tests/test_layering.py is
#                    what enforces the §0 split by asserting ib_async is absent
#                    from `decide`'s dependency tree.
#
#   README.md     -- pyproject.toml has `readme = "README.md"`, and uv sync
#                    builds this project itself, so hatchling reads it. This is
#                    why the doc exclusions above are listed one by one: a
#                    `*.md` line would take README.md with it.
#
#   LICENSE       -- pyproject.toml has `license = { file = "LICENSE" }`. The
#                    Dockerfile already carries a comment about this one: the
#                    build fails with "License file does not exist", which does
#                    not obviously point at a missing file in the context.
#
#   uv.lock       -- `uv sync --frozen` refuses to resolve without it.
#   pyproject.toml
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
